statement that smoke does not attest the production workload and that no production result is claimed before the real runs complete.\",\n      \"Search and final metrics.json (exact scalar sets), the declared aggregation hierarchy with weights, the plane-level mean rerun-agreement label (mean top-3 Jaccard) at the 4*d and 16*d budgets (mean_label_low_budget, mean_label_high_budget), and the conditions under which single-run Kernel SHAP is reliable, conditional or unreliable at that plane/budget level, reported as measured including negative and uncertain results; no per-dataset/model tables and no RBO or Nogueira stability are produced by the evaluators.\",\n      \"Comparisons of the candidate diagnostic with always_reliable, constant_half and split_half_gap_heuristic baselines (positive skill means lower MSE) with paired-bootstrap intervals, and the label_permuted_pairing control with confirmation that derangements were non-vacuous; incomplete or failed cases/controls reported with their worst-case contributions and never omitted or renormalized.\",\n      \"Statement of the enforcement distinction: the Kernel SHAP coalition budget per run is enforced by the trusted evaluator (the evaluator generates and counts coalitions), the wall-clock deadline and broker RPC cap are harness-enforced, and the candidate has no internal-operation counter that is trusted; candidate-reported counters, if any, are advisory only.\",\n      \"Frozen-candidate evidence: search ranking record of all evaluated candidates (at most 3 cycles x 1 evaluation), eligibility status, the deterministic selection and tie rule applied, and proof the candidate was unchanged at final time; explicit separation of scientific validity, search eligibility and final claim assessment.\",\n      \"Limitations statement: explainer variability considered only from coalition sampling (fixed 32-row background per cell, fixed trained model per episode), only 3 model families, 2 seeds per plane, k=3, interventiona