{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PA7rkPnERtAzV3Yojq9SFh","type":"tool_result","content":"# program_1 notes\n\n## What was implemented\n- Baseline-equivalent skeleton (8 folds over complement pairs, jackknife, simulated top-3 Jaccard).\n- Variance reduction: 1000 draws as 500 antithetic pairs, common random numbers per episode (seeded by reset seed).\n- `_jackknife_cov` gives centred, scaled delete-one-group deviations; full-covariance draws are `phi + mult * z @ dev` (sum(phi) constraint preserved since each replicate satisfies it).\n- `_sim_jaccard(phi, dev, mult, k, ...)` exposes the spread multiplier and diag/full-cov choice.\n- `_calibrate` maps features (sim Jaccard diag@1, diag@0.7, full@1, full@sqrt2, log2(B/d), tanh(margin z/3), family) with `_CALIB_COEF`, then final r = 0.7*calibrated + 0.3*diag@1, clipped to [0.02, 1].\n- Any per-instance exception or non-finite value falls back to 0.9.\n\n## IMPORTANT limitation: calibration constants are NOT fitted\nThis candidate was authored under a rule set forbidding executing any code (no Python, no local replica,\nno CV). The planned local replica (sklearn datasets, logreg/RF/MLP, B in {4d,16d}, 32 background rows,\n8 reruns, leave-one-dataset-out CV) was therefore NOT run. No held-out-CV MSE exists; none is claimed.\n`_CALIB_COEF` values are hand-set conservative priors: weights 0.5/0.2/0.3 on diag@1, diag@0.7, full@1\n(sum 1.0, so the map is a convex combination of simulators), zero weight on the sqrt(2)-inflated simulator,\nB/d, margin and family terms. Rationale: cycle-1 (inflation sqrt2 + full cov + 48 groups) scored below\nbaseline and labels skew high, so mild deflation / no inflation is the direction suggested; this is a\nhypothesis, not a result. Expected behaviour is close to the baseline with lower MC noise; the\nablation (variance-only vs +cov vs +inflation vs +calibration) remains to be done by running the\nreplica harness described in the idea plan.\n\n---\n# Cycle 3 (program_1): budget-aware empirical-Bayes shrinkage + partition-ensembled jackknife\nAttempt `c03_budget_prior_partition_ensemble_attempt_01`.\n\n## Changes vs cycle 2 (program_0)\n1. `_N_PARTITIONS = 4`: the delete-one-group jackknife is repeated over 4 independent random fold\n   partitions (`rng.permutation(pairs) % _FOLDS`, drawn from the reset-seeded generator); simulated\n   Jaccards (diag@1.0, diag@0.7, full-cov@1.0) and the margin z are averaged with `np.mean(sims, axis=0)`.\n   CRN/antithetic draws unchanged. Partitions with <2 valid folds are skipped; if none is valid -> prior.\n2. `_PRIOR_BY_RATIO = {2.0: 0.84, 4.0: 0.96}` keyed on log2(B/d), `_prior_for(B, d)` interpolates linearly, clips outside.\n3. `_empirical_bayes`: r = `_W_SIM`(0.6) * sim_combo + (1-`_W_SIM`) * prior, sim_combo = 0.5 s_d10 + 0.2 s_d07 + 0.3 s_f10\n   (the cycle-2 convex combination, so `_calibrate`/`_SHRINK` are no longer used in the output path).\n4. Soft margin gate: + `_MARGIN_BOOST`(0.02) * tanh(margin_z / `_MARGIN_SCALE`(3)); clip to [0.02, 1].\n5. Fallback on exception / non-finite -> budget prior (not constant 0.9; 0.9 only if B/d itself is unusable).\n\n## Provenance of constants (honest statement)\n- Prior values 0.84 / 0.96: aggregate label means by budget seen in earlier evaluation metrics (not instance labels,\n  not fitted by this code). `_W_SIM`, `_MARGIN_BOOST`, `_MARGIN_SCALE`, `_N_PARTITIONS`: hand-set, untuned.\n- No code was executed while writing this candidate (rules forbade it): no sanity run, no CV, no tuning. Correctness\n  of shapes/finiteness is by inspection only. Runtime estimate: 4 partitions x 9 lstsq solves + 3 sims per instance.\n- Planned ablation order if runs become possible: partition ensemble only, prior only, margin gate only; tune `_W_SIM` in {0.5, 0.6, 0.8}.\n- Risk: the prior encodes the budget-wise label mean from the search datasets; if held-out label means differ, the shrinkage may hurt.\n\"\"\"Candidate: calibrated, low-MC-noise rerun simulation for single-run Kernel SHAP reliability.\n\nInterface (python_rpc_v1:handle): ``handle(request) -> response`` with finite JSON-compatible\nvalues only.  Candidate state lives only in this module's memory; nothing is read from or written\nto evaluator paths.\n\nOperations\n----------\n{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int>}      -> exactly {\"ok\": true}; any non-negative integer seed.\n{\"op\": \"diagnose\", \"workload\": {...}, \"instances\": [...]}\n    workload: n_features d, n_masks B (4d or 16d, complement pairs adjacent), family\n    (\"logreg\" | \"random_forest\" | \"mlp\"), k (=3), n_instances.\n    instance keys: masks (bit-packed uint8, base64), weights (float64 [B]), values (float64 [B]),\n    anchors {\"empty\", \"full\"}.\n    Response: exactly {\"r_hat\": [float, ...]}, len == n_instances, finite, in [0, 1].\n\nMethod.  Same skeleton as the baseline: delete-one-group jackknife over complement pairs, then\nsimulate reruns by drawing attributions around the observed run and averaging the Jaccard overlap\nof the simulated top-k sets with the observed one.  Differences from the baseline, each kept\nseparate and individually switchable so they can be ablated:\n  1. Monte-Carlo noise reduction: 1000 draws (500 antithetic pairs) with common random numbers\n     fixed per episode via np.random.default_rng(seed).\n  2. A full-covariance simulator (``_jackknife_cov``; draws are phi + L z with L built from the\n     centred delete-one-group replicates, so the sum(phi) constraint is preserved) next to the\n     baseline diagonal simulator; spread multiplier ``mult`` is a parameter of ``_sim_jaccard``.\n  3. A small monotone ``_calibrate`` map (``_CALIB_COEF``) over the simulated Jaccards at several\n     spread multipliers, log2(B/d), a standardised top-k margin and the family, shrunk toward the\n     baseline-equivalent diagonal simulator.  See NOTES.md for how the constants were chosen.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_STATE = {\"rng\": np.random.default_rng(0), \"ready\": False, \"seed\": 0}\n_FOLDS = 8\n_N_DRAWS = 1000  # even: antithetic pairs\n_FALLBACK = 0.9  # only used if B/d is unavailable; otherwise the budget prior is the fallback\n_N_PARTITIONS = 4  # independent random fold partitions averaged per instance\n\n# Budget-specific prior means keyed on log2(B/d): 2 -> B=4d, 4 -> B=16d.  Hand-set from the\n# aggregate low/high-budget label means reported in earlier evaluation metrics (~0.84, ~0.96);\n# NOT fitted on instance data.  Interpolated linearly in log2(B/d) and clipped outside [2, 4].\n_PRIOR_BY_RATIO = {2.0: 0.84, 4.0: 0.96}\n_W_SIM = 0.6  # empirical-Bayes weight on the simulated-rerun reliability (1 - _W_SIM on the prior)\n_MARGIN_BOOST = 0.02  # coefficient of the soft margin gate\n_MARGIN_SCALE = 3.0\n\n# Calibration map: logit-free linear map on simulated Jaccards, clipped to [0, 1].\n# Features: s_d10 (diag, mult 1.0), s_d07 (diag, mult 0.7), s_f10 (full cov, mult 1.0),\n# s_f141 (full cov, mult sqrt(2)), lbd = log2(B/d) - 3 (0 at B=8d midpoint), mz = tanh(margin z / 3),\n# and family indicators.  The constants are conservative PRIORS (see NOTES.md): they were NOT\n# fitted on a local replica because no code could be executed while writing this candidate.\n# Cycle-1 evidence (spread inflation > 1 lowered the score; labels skew high) motivates putting\n# weight on the un-inflated / deflated simulators and none on the inflated one.\n_CALIB_COEF = {\n    \"intercept\": 0.0,\n    \"s_d10\": 0.50,\n    \"s_d07\": 0.20,\n    \"s_f10\": 0.30,\n    \"s_f141\": 0.0,\n    \"lbd\": 0.0,\n    \"mz\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_logreg\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_random_forest\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_mlp\": 0.0,\n}\n\n\ndef _decode(obj, dtype):\n    raw = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"].encode(\"ascii\"))\n    return np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=dtype).reshape(obj[\"shape\"])\n\n\ndef _solve(Z, w, v, v0, v1):\n    total = v1 - v0\n    A = Z[:, :-1] - Z[:, -1:]\n    t = (v - v0) - Z[:, -1] * total\n    sw = np.sqrt(w)\n    sol = np.linalg.lstsq(A * sw[:, None], t * sw, rcond=None)[0]\n    return np.append(sol, total - sol.sum())\n\n\ndef _top(a, k):\n    return np.argsort(-a, kind=\"stable\")[:k]\n\n\ndef _jackknife_cov(Z, w, v, v0, v1, fold_of_row, n_folds):\n    \"\"\"Delete-one-group jackknife over complement pairs.\n\n    Returns (phi, loo, dev, n): the full-data solution, the stacked leave-group-out solutions,\n    their centred deviations scaled so that dev.T @ dev is the jackknife covariance, and n.\n    \"\"\"\n    phi = _solve(Z, w, v, v0, v1)\n    d = Z.shape[1]\n    loo = []\n    for f in range(n_folds):\n        keep = fold_of_row != f\n        if keep.sum() > d:\n            loo.append(_solve(Z[keep], w[keep], v[keep], v0, v1))\n    if len(loo) < 2:\n        return phi, None, None, 0\n    loo = np.array(loo)\n    n = len(loo)\n    dev = np.sqrt((n - 1) / n) * (loo - loo.mean(0))\n    return phi, loo, dev, n\n\n\ndef _topk_mask(a, k):\n    idx = np.argsort(-a, axis=1, kind=\"stable\")[:, :k]\n    m = np.zeros(a.shape, dtype=bool)\n    np.put_along_axis(m, idx, True, axis=1)\n    return m\n\n\ndef _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, mult, k, z_full, z_diag, full_cov):\n    \"\"\"Mean Jaccard of simulated top-k sets vs the observed top-k set.\n\n    z_full: (N, n) common random numbers for the full-covariance draw; z_diag: (N, d) for the\n    diagonal draw.  ``mult`` scales the simulated spread.\n    \"\"\"\n    if full_cov:\n        noise = z_full[:, : dev.shape[0]] @ dev\n    else:\n        sd = np.sqrt((dev ** 2).sum(0))\n        noise = z_diag * sd[None, :]\n    draws = phi[None, :] + mult * noise\n    ref = np.zeros(phi.shape[0], dtype=bool)\n    ref[_top(np.abs(phi), k)] = True\n    sim = _topk_mask(np.abs(draws), k)\n    c = (sim & ref[None, :]).sum(1).astype(float)\n    return float(np.mean(c / (2 * k - c)))\n\n\ndef _margin_z(phi, loo, k):\n    \"\"\"Standardised gap between the k-th and (k+1)-th largest |phi| using the jackknife SE.\"\"\"\n    order = np.argsort(-np.abs(phi), kind=\"stable\")\n    if len(order) <= k:\n        return 3.0\n    a, b = order[k - 1], order[k]\n    gap = abs(phi[a]) - abs(phi[b])\n    g = np.abs(loo[:, a]) - np.abs(loo[:, b])\n    n = len(g)\n    se = np.sqrt((n - 1) / n * ((g - g.mean()) ** 2).sum())\n    return float(gap / max(se, 1e-12))\n\n\ndef _calibrate(feats, B, d, family):\n    c = _CALIB_COEF\n    lbd = np.log2(B / d) - 3.0\n    mz = np.tanh(feats[\"margin_z\"] / 3.0)\n    r = (c[\"intercept\"] + c[\"s_d10\"] * feats[\"s_d10\"] + c[\"s_d07\"] * feats[\"s_d07\"]\n         + c[\"s_f10\"] * feats[\"s_f10\"] + c[\"s_f141\"] * feats[\"s_f141\"]\n         + c[\"lbd\"] * lbd + c[\"mz\"] * mz + c.get(\"fam_\" + str(family), 0.0))\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.0, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _prior_for(B, d):\n    \"\"\"Budget prior mean, linear in log2(B/d) between the two anchors, clipped outside.\"\"\"\n    xs = sorted(_PRIOR_BY_RATIO)\n    ys = [_PRIOR_BY_RATIO[x] for x in xs]\n    return float(np.interp(np.log2(B / d), xs, ys))\n\n\ndef _empirical_bayes(sim_combo, prior, margin_z):\n    \"\"\"Shrink the simulated-rerun reliability toward the budget prior, then soft margin gate.\"\"\"\n    r = _W_SIM * sim_combo + (1.0 - _W_SIM) * prior\n    r = r + _MARGIN_BOOST * np.tanh(margin_z / _MARGIN_SCALE)\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.02, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _diagnose_one(inst, d, B, k, family, rng, z_full, z_diag):\n    prior = _prior_for(B, d)\n    Z = np.unpackbits(_decode(inst[\"masks\"], np.uint8), axis=1, count=d, bitorder=\"little\").astype(float)\n    w = _decode(inst[\"weights\"], \"<f8\").astype(float)\n    v = _decode(inst[\"values\"], \"<f8\").astype(float)\n    v0, v1 = float(inst[\"anchors\"][\"empty\"]), float(inst[\"anchors\"][\"full\"])\n    pairs = (B + 1) // 2\n    sims = []\n    mzs = []\n    for _p in range(_N_PARTITIONS):\n        fold = rng.permutation(pairs) % _FOLDS\n        fold_of_row = np.repeat(fold, 2)[:B]\n        phi, loo, dev, n = _jackknife_cov(Z, w, v, v0, v1, fold_of_row, _FOLDS)\n        if loo is None:\n            continue\n        s_d10 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 1.0, k, z_full, z_diag, False)\n        s_d07 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 0.7, k, z_full, z_diag, False)\n        s_f10 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 1.0, k, z_full, z_diag, True)\n        mz = _margin_z(phi, loo, k)\n        row = [s_d10, s_d07, s_f10, mz]\n        if all(np.isfinite(x) for x in row):\n            sims.append(row)\n    if not sims:\n        return prior\n    m = np.mean(sims, axis=0)\n    c = _CALIB_COEF\n    sim_combo = c[\"s_d10\"] * m[0] + c[\"s_d07\"] * m[1] + c[\"s_f10\"] * m[2]\n    r = _empirical_bayes(sim_combo, prior, float(m[3]))\n    if not np.isfinite(r):\n        return prior\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.02, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _crn(seed, d):\n    \"\"\"Common random numbers fixed per episode (antithetic pairs).\"\"\"\n    g = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    half = _N_DRAWS // 2\n    zf = g.standard_normal((half, _FOLDS))\n    zd = g.standard_normal((half, d))\n    return np.concatenate([zf, -zf]), np.concatenate([zd, -zd])\n\n\ndef _safe_prior(B, d):\n    try:\n        p = _prior_for(B, d)\n        return p if np.isfinite(p) else _FALLBACK\n    except Exception:\n        return _FALLBACK\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    op = request.get(\"op\")\n    if op == \"reset\":\n        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n        _STATE[\"ready\"] = True\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"diagnose\":\n        wl = request[\"workload\"]\n        d, B, k = int(wl[\"n_features\"]), int(wl[\"n_masks\"]), int(wl[\"k\"])\n        family = wl.get(\"family\", \"\")\n        rng = _STATE[\"rng\"]\n        z_full, z_diag = _crn(_STATE[\"seed\"], d)\n        out = []\n        for inst in request[\"instances\"]:\n            try:\n                r = _diagnose_one(inst, d, B, k, family, rng, z_full, z_diag)\n            except Exception:\n                r = _safe_prior(B, d)\n            if not np.isfinite(r):\n                r = _safe_prior(B, d)\n            out.append(float(np.clip(r, 0.0, 1.0)))\n        return {\"r_hat\": out}\n    raise ValueError(\"unsupported op\")\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\n{\n  \"completed_at\": \"2026-11-11T08:06:54.969546+00:00\",\n  \"compute_usage\": {\n    \"elapsed_seconds\": 131.9684356899961,\n    \"max_rpc_calls\": 74,\n    \"objective_counts\": \"advisory\",\n    \"outcome\": \"completed\",\n    \"rpc_calls\": 72,\n    \"wall_clock_limit_seconds\": 4500\n  },\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"declared_final_metrics\": [\n    \"combined_score\",\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable\",\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half\",\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n    \"control_permuted_score\",\n    \"spearman_r_hat_vs_label\",\n    \"mean_label_low_budget\",\n    \"mean_label_high_budget\",\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable_ci_low\",\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\",\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\",\n    \"combined_minus_control_ci_low\"\n  ],\n  \"evaluation_evidence\": {\n    \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\": \"unverified\",\n    \"episode_count\": 2,\n    \"sha256\": \"sha256:ab384773fb7dd6e568ed07eec6ed7b328de962b2b0c1e04a99e98d91b81951fd\",\n    \"status\": \"available\"\n  },\n  \"evaluator_sha256\": \"sha256:08c6a3cf5c89564da1dc3431cd4e8849ed1a70e0ca5748ac28f35c2740e8514e\",\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"combined_minus_control_ci_low\": 0.010062970031696823,\n    \"combined_score\": 0.9837903000065031,\n    \"control_permuted_score\": 0.9700566732219201,\n    \"mean_label_high_budget\": 0.9315277777777777,\n    \"mean_label_low_budget\": 0.8065277777777778,\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable\": 0.035288129867614246,\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable_ci_low\": 0.01713659700405952,\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half\": 0.15431590764539205,\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\": 0.1245256118853025,\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic\": 0.012198633276915734,\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\": 0.008117269655327863,\n    \"spearman_r_hat_vs_label\": 0.5808649073155919\n  },\n  \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n  \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:b4f9b3282c7754c82e74076955653f613a6ee1900a3476a716bb0641dcce90ea\",\n  \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:7a7c88ba8f1761377037cac5b899efccc6ae2872da25b046d7c7141b968247d7\",\n  \"schema_version\": 3,\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a0aea7f-e3c0-4bf6-b0cd-dac6f7fb95fd","uuid":"35206fda-4223-4ad5-8476-955afb6b7a81","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:12:45.135Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# program_1 notes\n\n## What was implemented\n- Baseline-equivalent skeleton (8 folds over complement pairs, jackknife, simulated top-3 Jaccard).\n- Variance reduction: 1000 draws as 500 antithetic pairs, common random numbers per episode (seeded by reset seed).\n- `_jackknife_cov` gives centred, scaled delete-one-group deviations; full-covariance draws are `phi + mult * z @ dev` (sum(phi) constraint preserved since each replicate satisfies it).\n- `_sim_jaccard(phi, dev, mult, k, ...)` exposes the spread multiplier and diag/full-cov choice.\n- `_calibrate` maps features (sim Jaccard diag@1, diag@0.7, full@1, full@sqrt2, log2(B/d), tanh(margin z/3), family) with `_CALIB_COEF`, then final r = 0.7*calibrated + 0.3*diag@1, clipped to [0.02, 1].\n- Any per-instance exception or non-finite value falls back to 0.9.\n\n## IMPORTANT limitation: calibration constants are NOT fitted\nThis candidate was authored under a rule set forbidding executing any code (no Python, no local replica,\nno CV). The planned local replica (sklearn datasets, logreg/RF/MLP, B in {4d,16d}, 32 background rows,\n8 reruns, leave-one-dataset-out CV) was therefore NOT run. No held-out-CV MSE exists; none is claimed.\n`_CALIB_COEF` values are hand-set conservative priors: weights 0.5/0.2/0.3 on diag@1, diag@0.7, full@1\n(sum 1.0, so the map is a convex combination of simulators), zero weight on the sqrt(2)-inflated simulator,\nB/d, margin and family terms. Rationale: cycle-1 (inflation sqrt2 + full cov + 48 groups) scored below\nbaseline and labels skew high, so mild deflation / no inflation is the direction suggested; this is a\nhypothesis, not a result. Expected behaviour is close to the baseline with lower MC noise; the\nablation (variance-only vs +cov vs +inflation vs +calibration) remains to be done by running the\nreplica harness described in the idea plan.\n\n---\n# Cycle 3 (program_1): budget-aware empirical-Bayes shrinkage + partition-ensembled jackknife\nAttempt `c03_budget_prior_partition_ensemble_attempt_01`.\n\n## Changes vs cycle 2 (program_0)\n1. `_N_PARTITIONS = 4`: the delete-one-group jackknife is repeated over 4 independent random fold\n   partitions (`rng.permutation(pairs) % _FOLDS`, drawn from the reset-seeded generator); simulated\n   Jaccards (diag@1.0, diag@0.7, full-cov@1.0) and the margin z are averaged with `np.mean(sims, axis=0)`.\n   CRN/antithetic draws unchanged. Partitions with <2 valid folds are skipped; if none is valid -> prior.\n2. `_PRIOR_BY_RATIO = {2.0: 0.84, 4.0: 0.96}` keyed on log2(B/d), `_prior_for(B, d)` interpolates linearly, clips outside.\n3. `_empirical_bayes`: r = `_W_SIM`(0.6) * sim_combo + (1-`_W_SIM`) * prior, sim_combo = 0.5 s_d10 + 0.2 s_d07 + 0.3 s_f10\n   (the cycle-2 convex combination, so `_calibrate`/`_SHRINK` are no longer used in the output path).\n4. Soft margin gate: + `_MARGIN_BOOST`(0.02) * tanh(margin_z / `_MARGIN_SCALE`(3)); clip to [0.02, 1].\n5. Fallback on exception / non-finite -> budget prior (not constant 0.9; 0.9 only if B/d itself is unusable).\n\n## Provenance of constants (honest statement)\n- Prior values 0.84 / 0.96: aggregate label means by budget seen in earlier evaluation metrics (not instance labels,\n  not fitted by this code). `_W_SIM`, `_MARGIN_BOOST`, `_MARGIN_SCALE`, `_N_PARTITIONS`: hand-set, untuned.\n- No code was executed while writing this candidate (rules forbade it): no sanity run, no CV, no tuning. Correctness\n  of shapes/finiteness is by inspection only. Runtime estimate: 4 partitions x 9 lstsq solves + 3 sims per instance.\n- Planned ablation order if runs become possible: partition ensemble only, prior only, margin gate only; tune `_W_SIM` in {0.5, 0.6, 0.8}.\n- Risk: the prior encodes the budget-wise label mean from the search datasets; if held-out label means differ, the shrinkage may hurt.\n\"\"\"Candidate: calibrated, low-MC-noise rerun simulation for single-run Kernel SHAP reliability.\n\nInterface (python_rpc_v1:handle): ``handle(request) -> response`` with finite JSON-compatible\nvalues only.  Candidate state lives only in this module's memory; nothing is read from or written\nto evaluator paths.\n\nOperations\n----------\n{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int>}      -> exactly {\"ok\": true}; any non-negative integer seed.\n{\"op\": \"diagnose\", \"workload\": {...}, \"instances\": [...]}\n    workload: n_features d, n_masks B (4d or 16d, complement pairs adjacent), family\n    (\"logreg\" | \"random_forest\" | \"mlp\"), k (=3), n_instances.\n    instance keys: masks (bit-packed uint8, base64), weights (float64 [B]), values (float64 [B]),\n    anchors {\"empty\", \"full\"}.\n    Response: exactly {\"r_hat\": [float, ...]}, len == n_instances, finite, in [0, 1].\n\nMethod.  Same skeleton as the baseline: delete-one-group jackknife over complement pairs, then\nsimulate reruns by drawing attributions around the observed run and averaging the Jaccard overlap\nof the simulated top-k sets with the observed one.  Differences from the baseline, each kept\nseparate and individually switchable so they can be ablated:\n  1. Monte-Carlo noise reduction: 1000 draws (500 antithetic pairs) with common random numbers\n     fixed per episode via np.random.default_rng(seed).\n  2. A full-covariance simulator (``_jackknife_cov``; draws are phi + L z with L built from the\n     centred delete-one-group replicates, so the sum(phi) constraint is preserved) next to the\n     baseline diagonal simulator; spread multiplier ``mult`` is a parameter of ``_sim_jaccard``.\n  3. A small monotone ``_calibrate`` map (``_CALIB_COEF``) over the simulated Jaccards at several\n     spread multipliers, log2(B/d), a standardised top-k margin and the family, shrunk toward the\n     baseline-equivalent diagonal simulator.  See NOTES.md for how the constants were chosen.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_STATE = {\"rng\": np.random.default_rng(0), \"ready\": False, \"seed\": 0}\n_FOLDS = 8\n_N_DRAWS = 1000  # even: antithetic pairs\n_FALLBACK = 0.9  # only used if B/d is unavailable; otherwise the budget prior is the fallback\n_N_PARTITIONS = 4  # independent random fold partitions averaged per instance\n\n# Budget-specific prior means keyed on log2(B/d): 2 -> B=4d, 4 -> B=16d.  Hand-set from the\n# aggregate low/high-budget label means reported in earlier evaluation metrics (~0.84, ~0.96);\n# NOT fitted on instance data.  Interpolated linearly in log2(B/d) and clipped outside [2, 4].\n_PRIOR_BY_RATIO = {2.0: 0.84, 4.0: 0.96}\n_W_SIM = 0.6  # empirical-Bayes weight on the simulated-rerun reliability (1 - _W_SIM on the prior)\n_MARGIN_BOOST = 0.02  # coefficient of the soft margin gate\n_MARGIN_SCALE = 3.0\n\n# Calibration map: logit-free linear map on simulated Jaccards, clipped to [0, 1].\n# Features: s_d10 (diag, mult 1.0), s_d07 (diag, mult 0.7), s_f10 (full cov, mult 1.0),\n# s_f141 (full cov, mult sqrt(2)), lbd = log2(B/d) - 3 (0 at B=8d midpoint), mz = tanh(margin z / 3),\n# and family indicators.  The constants are conservative PRIORS (see NOTES.md): they were NOT\n# fitted on a local replica because no code could be executed while writing this candidate.\n# Cycle-1 evidence (spread inflation > 1 lowered the score; labels skew high) motivates putting\n# weight on the un-inflated / deflated simulators and none on the inflated one.\n_CALIB_COEF = {\n    \"intercept\": 0.0,\n    \"s_d10\": 0.50,\n    \"s_d07\": 0.20,\n    \"s_f10\": 0.30,\n    \"s_f141\": 0.0,\n    \"lbd\": 0.0,\n    \"mz\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_logreg\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_random_forest\": 0.0,\n    \"fam_mlp\": 0.0,\n}\n\n\ndef _decode(obj, dtype):\n    raw = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"].encode(\"ascii\"))\n    return np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=dtype).reshape(obj[\"shape\"])\n\n\ndef _solve(Z, w, v, v0, v1):\n    total = v1 - v0\n    A = Z[:, :-1] - Z[:, -1:]\n    t = (v - v0) - Z[:, -1] * total\n    sw = np.sqrt(w)\n    sol = np.linalg.lstsq(A * sw[:, None], t * sw, rcond=None)[0]\n    return np.append(sol, total - sol.sum())\n\n\ndef _top(a, k):\n    return np.argsort(-a, kind=\"stable\")[:k]\n\n\ndef _jackknife_cov(Z, w, v, v0, v1, fold_of_row, n_folds):\n    \"\"\"Delete-one-group jackknife over complement pairs.\n\n    Returns (phi, loo, dev, n): the full-data solution, the stacked leave-group-out solutions,\n    their centred deviations scaled so that dev.T @ dev is the jackknife covariance, and n.\n    \"\"\"\n    phi = _solve(Z, w, v, v0, v1)\n    d = Z.shape[1]\n    loo = []\n    for f in range(n_folds):\n        keep = fold_of_row != f\n        if keep.sum() > d:\n            loo.append(_solve(Z[keep], w[keep], v[keep], v0, v1))\n    if len(loo) < 2:\n        return phi, None, None, 0\n    loo = np.array(loo)\n    n = len(loo)\n    dev = np.sqrt((n - 1) / n) * (loo - loo.mean(0))\n    return phi, loo, dev, n\n\n\ndef _topk_mask(a, k):\n    idx = np.argsort(-a, axis=1, kind=\"stable\")[:, :k]\n    m = np.zeros(a.shape, dtype=bool)\n    np.put_along_axis(m, idx, True, axis=1)\n    return m\n\n\ndef _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, mult, k, z_full, z_diag, full_cov):\n    \"\"\"Mean Jaccard of simulated top-k sets vs the observed top-k set.\n\n    z_full: (N, n) common random numbers for the full-covariance draw; z_diag: (N, d) for the\n    diagonal draw.  ``mult`` scales the simulated spread.\n    \"\"\"\n    if full_cov:\n        noise = z_full[:, : dev.shape[0]] @ dev\n    else:\n        sd = np.sqrt((dev ** 2).sum(0))\n        noise = z_diag * sd[None, :]\n    draws = phi[None, :] + mult * noise\n    ref = np.zeros(phi.shape[0], dtype=bool)\n    ref[_top(np.abs(phi), k)] = True\n    sim = _topk_mask(np.abs(draws), k)\n    c = (sim & ref[None, :]).sum(1).astype(float)\n    return float(np.mean(c / (2 * k - c)))\n\n\ndef _margin_z(phi, loo, k):\n    \"\"\"Standardised gap between the k-th and (k+1)-th largest |phi| using the jackknife SE.\"\"\"\n    order = np.argsort(-np.abs(phi), kind=\"stable\")\n    if len(order) <= k:\n        return 3.0\n    a, b = order[k - 1], order[k]\n    gap = abs(phi[a]) - abs(phi[b])\n    g = np.abs(loo[:, a]) - np.abs(loo[:, b])\n    n = len(g)\n    se = np.sqrt((n - 1) / n * ((g - g.mean()) ** 2).sum())\n    return float(gap / max(se, 1e-12))\n\n\ndef _calibrate(feats, B, d, family):\n    c = _CALIB_COEF\n    lbd = np.log2(B / d) - 3.0\n    mz = np.tanh(feats[\"margin_z\"] / 3.0)\n    r = (c[\"intercept\"] + c[\"s_d10\"] * feats[\"s_d10\"] + c[\"s_d07\"] * feats[\"s_d07\"]\n         + c[\"s_f10\"] * feats[\"s_f10\"] + c[\"s_f141\"] * feats[\"s_f141\"]\n         + c[\"lbd\"] * lbd + c[\"mz\"] * mz + c.get(\"fam_\" + str(family), 0.0))\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.0, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _prior_for(B, d):\n    \"\"\"Budget prior mean, linear in log2(B/d) between the two anchors, clipped outside.\"\"\"\n    xs = sorted(_PRIOR_BY_RATIO)\n    ys = [_PRIOR_BY_RATIO[x] for x in xs]\n    return float(np.interp(np.log2(B / d), xs, ys))\n\n\ndef _empirical_bayes(sim_combo, prior, margin_z):\n    \"\"\"Shrink the simulated-rerun reliability toward the budget prior, then soft margin gate.\"\"\"\n    r = _W_SIM * sim_combo + (1.0 - _W_SIM) * prior\n    r = r + _MARGIN_BOOST * np.tanh(margin_z / _MARGIN_SCALE)\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.02, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _diagnose_one(inst, d, B, k, family, rng, z_full, z_diag):\n    prior = _prior_for(B, d)\n    Z = np.unpackbits(_decode(inst[\"masks\"], np.uint8), axis=1, count=d, bitorder=\"little\").astype(float)\n    w = _decode(inst[\"weights\"], \"<f8\").astype(float)\n    v = _decode(inst[\"values\"], \"<f8\").astype(float)\n    v0, v1 = float(inst[\"anchors\"][\"empty\"]), float(inst[\"anchors\"][\"full\"])\n    pairs = (B + 1) // 2\n    sims = []\n    mzs = []\n    for _p in range(_N_PARTITIONS):\n        fold = rng.permutation(pairs) % _FOLDS\n        fold_of_row = np.repeat(fold, 2)[:B]\n        phi, loo, dev, n = _jackknife_cov(Z, w, v, v0, v1, fold_of_row, _FOLDS)\n        if loo is None:\n            continue\n        s_d10 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 1.0, k, z_full, z_diag, False)\n        s_d07 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 0.7, k, z_full, z_diag, False)\n        s_f10 = _sim_jaccard(phi, dev, 1.0, k, z_full, z_diag, True)\n        mz = _margin_z(phi, loo, k)\n        row = [s_d10, s_d07, s_f10, mz]\n        if all(np.isfinite(x) for x in row):\n            sims.append(row)\n    if not sims:\n        return prior\n    m = np.mean(sims, axis=0)\n    c = _CALIB_COEF\n    sim_combo = c[\"s_d10\"] * m[0] + c[\"s_d07\"] * m[1] + c[\"s_f10\"] * m[2]\n    r = _empirical_bayes(sim_combo, prior, float(m[3]))\n    if not np.isfinite(r):\n        return prior\n    return float(np.clip(r, 0.02, 1.0))\n\n\ndef _crn(seed, d):\n    \"\"\"Common random numbers fixed per episode (antithetic pairs).\"\"\"\n    g = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    half = _N_DRAWS // 2\n    zf = g.standard_normal((half, _FOLDS))\n    zd = g.standard_normal((half, d))\n    return np.concatenate([zf, -zf]), np.concatenate([zd, -zd])\n\n\ndef _safe_prior(B, d):\n    try:\n        p = _prior_for(B, d)\n        return p if np.isfinite(p) else _FALLBACK\n    except Exception:\n        return _FALLBACK\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    op = request.get(\"op\")\n    if op == \"reset\":\n        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n        _STATE[\"ready\"] = True\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"diagnose\":\n        wl = request[\"workload\"]\n        d, B, k = int(wl[\"n_features\"]), int(wl[\"n_masks\"]), int(wl[\"k\"])\n        family = wl.get(\"family\", \"\")\n        rng = _STATE[\"rng\"]\n        z_full, z_diag = _crn(_STATE[\"seed\"], d)\n        out = []\n        for inst in request[\"instances\"]:\n            try:\n                r = _diagnose_one(inst, d, B, k, family, rng, z_full, z_diag)\n            except Exception:\n                r = _safe_prior(B, d)\n            if not np.isfinite(r):\n                r = _safe_prior(B, d)\n            out.append(float(np.clip(r, 0.0, 1.0)))\n        return {\"r_hat\": out}\n    raise ValueError(\"unsupported op\")\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\n{\n  \"completed_at\": \"2026-11-11T08:06:54.969546+00:00\",\n  \"compute_usage\": {\n    \"elapsed_seconds\": 131.9684356899961,\n    \"max_rpc_calls\": 74,\n    \"objective_counts\": \"advisory\",\n    \"outcome\": \"completed\",\n    \"rpc_calls\": 72,\n    \"wall_clock_limit_seconds\": 4500\n  },\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"declared_final_metrics\": [\n    \"combined_score\",\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable\",\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half\",\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic\",\n    \"control_permuted_score\",\n    \"spearman_r_hat_vs_label\",\n    \"mean_label_low_budget\",\n    \"mean_label_high_budget\",\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable_ci_low\",\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\",\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\",\n    \"combined_minus_control_ci_low\"\n  ],\n  \"evaluation_evidence\": {\n    \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\": \"unverified\",\n    \"episode_count\": 2,\n    \"sha256\": \"sha256:ab384773fb7dd6e568ed07eec6ed7b328de962b2b0c1e04a99e98d91b81951fd\",\n    \"status\": \"available\"\n  },\n  \"evaluator_sha256\": \"sha256:08c6a3cf5c89564da1dc3431cd4e8849ed1a70e0ca5748ac28f35c2740e8514e\",\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"combined_minus_control_ci_low\": 0.010062970031696823,\n    \"combined_score\": 0.9837903000065031,\n    \"control_permuted_score\": 0.9700566732219201,\n    \"mean_label_high_budget\": 0.9315277777777777,\n    \"mean_label_low_budget\": 0.8065277777777778,\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable\": 0.035288129867614246,\n    \"skill_vs_always_reliable_ci_low\": 0.01713659700405952,\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half\": 0.15431590764539205,\n    \"skill_vs_constant_half_ci_low\": 0.1245256118853025,\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic\": 0.012198633276915734,\n    \"skill_vs_gap_heuristic_ci_low\": 0.008117269655327863,\n    \"spearman_r_hat_vs_label\": 0.5808649073155919\n  },\n  \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n  \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:b4f9b3282c7754c82e74076955653f613a6ee1900a3476a716bb0641dcce90ea\",\n  \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:7a7c88ba8f1761377037cac5b899efccc6ae2872da25b046d7c7141b968247d7\",\n  \"schema_version\": 3,","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
